1-# Long-term Memory
2-
3-Long-term memory is **persistent**, **cross-session** storage designed for knowledge that should be retained and searchable across all interactions. It's the "knowledge base" of facts, preferences, and experiences the agent learns at runtime.
4-
5-## Overview
6-
7:Long-term memory provides persistent storage that survives server restarts and session expiration. It's optimized for semantic, keyword, and hybrid search, deduplication, and rich metadata to enable intelligent retrieval of relevant information.
8-
9-| Feature | Details |
10-|---------|---------|
11-| **Scope** | Cross-session, persistent |
12-| **Lifespan** | Permanent until manually deleted |
13-| **Storage** | Redis with vector and full-text indexing |
14-| **Search** | Semantic, keyword, and hybrid search |
15-| **Capacity** | Unlimited (with compaction) |
16-| **Use Case** | Knowledge base, user preferences |
17-| **Indexing** | Vector embeddings + full-text index + metadata |
18:| **Deduplication** | Hash-based and semantic |
19-
20-## Characteristics
21-
22-- **Cross-Session**: Accessible from any session
23-- **Persistent**: Survives server restarts and session expiration
24-- **Multi-Modal Search**: Semantic (vector), keyword (BM25 full-text), and hybrid search — configurable embeddings (OpenAI, Bedrock, Ollama, and more via [LiteLLM](llm-providers.md))
25:- **Deduplication**: Automatic hash-based and semantic deduplication
26-- **Rich Metadata**: Topics, entities, timestamps, memory types
27-- **Compaction**: Automatic cleanup and merging of duplicates
28-
29-## Memory Types
30-
31-Long-term memory supports three types of memories:
32-
33-### 1. Semantic Memory
34-Facts, preferences, general knowledge
35-
36-```json
37-{
38-  "text": "User prefers dark mode interfaces",
39:  "memory_type": "semantic",
40-  "topics": ["preferences", "ui"],
41-  "entities": ["dark mode"]
42-}
43-```
44-
45-### 2. Episodic Memory
46-Events with temporal context
47-
48-```json
49-{
50-  "text": "User visited Paris in March 2024",
51-  "memory_type": "episodic",
52-  "event_date": "2024-03-15T10:00:00Z",
53-  "topics": ["travel"],
54-  "entities": ["Paris"]
55-}
56-```
57-
58-### 3. Message Memory
59-Conversation records (auto-generated)
60-
61-```json
62-{
63-  "text": "user: What's the weather like?",
64-  "memory_type": "message",
65-  "session_id": "chat_123"
66-}
67-```
68-
69-## When to Use Long-Term Memory
70-
71-### 1. User Preferences and Profile
72-
73-```python
74-# Store lasting user preferences
75-memories = [
76-    MemoryRecord(
77-        text="User prefers metric units for temperature",
78-        id="pref_metric_temp",
79:        memory_type="semantic",
80-        topics=["preferences", "units"],
81-        user_id="user_123"
82-    )
83-]
84-```
85-
86-### 2. Important Facts and Knowledge
87-
88-```python
89-# Store domain knowledge
90-memories = [
91-    MemoryRecord(
92-        text="Customer's subscription expires on 2024-06-15",
93-        id="sub_expiry_customer_456",
94-        memory_type="episodic",
95-        event_date=datetime(2024, 6, 15),
96-        entities=["customer_456", "subscription"],
97-        user_id="user_123"
98-    )
99-]
100-```
101-
102-### 3. Cross-Session Context
103-
104-```python
105-# Store context that spans conversations
106-memories = [
107-    MemoryRecord(
108-        text="User is working on a Python machine learning project",
109-        id="context_ml_project",
110:        memory_type="semantic",
111-        topics=["programming", "machine-learning", "python"],
112-        namespace="work_context"
113-    )
114-]
115-```
116-
117-## API Endpoints
118-
119-```http
120-# Create long-term memories
121-POST /v1/long-term-memory/
122-
123-# Search long-term memories
124-POST /v1/long-term-memory/search
125-```
126-
127-## Search Capabilities
128-
129:Long-term memory supports three search modes: **semantic** (vector similarity), **keyword** (full-text matching), and **hybrid** (combined).
130-
131-### Semantic Search (Default)
132-```json
133-{
134-  "text": "python programming help",
135:  "search_mode": "semantic",
136-  "limit": 10,
137-  "distance_threshold": 0.8
138-}
139-```
140-
141-### Keyword Search
142-```json
143-{
144-  "text": "TechCorp engineer",
145-  "search_mode": "keyword",
146-  "limit": 10
147-}
148-```
149-
150-### Hybrid Search
151:Combines vector similarity with full-text keyword matching. Use `hybrid_alpha` to control the balance (0.0 = pure keyword, 1.0 = pure semantic, default 0.7).
152-```json
153-{
154-  "text": "python programming help",
155-  "search_mode": "hybrid",
156-  "hybrid_alpha": 0.7,
157-  "limit": 10
158-}
159-```
160-

